# i18n readability follow-up (named constants, worked examples)

Context: A readability review of the English/Korean UI internationalisation
found raw DOM node-type numbers, an unnamed cookie lifetime, a fallback chain
in translateWith without examples, an implicit else branch in the mutation
observer, and an environment variable read twice. No behaviour change.

Changes:

1. src/front/static/global/js/i18n.js
   Node.ELEMENT_NODE / TEXT_NODE / DOCUMENT_NODE / DOCUMENT_FRAGMENT_NODE
   instead of raw numbers (read only inside DOM functions, so the node test
   harness still works); ONE_YEAR_SECONDS for the ob_lang cookie max-age;
   one input -> output example per translateWith fallback branch; explicit
   characterData / attributes branch in observe(); keep-in-sync comment
   pointing to dependencies.py.
2. src/front/fastapi/dependencies.py
   ONTOBRICKS_UI_LANG read once into _ENV_UI_LANG; keep-in-sync comment
   pointing to i18n.js.

Modified files:
- src/front/static/global/js/i18n.js
- src/front/fastapi/dependencies.py

Tests: `uv run --frozen pytest -q -p no:cacheprovider tests/units/front`
-> 1074 passed; node --check i18n.js OK.

# i18n review fixes (PR #196): skip regions, lazy dictionary, docs, tests

Context: Maintainer review of the English/Korean UI internationalisation asked
that user-authored content never be matched against the dictionary, that the
~281 KB Korean dictionary not load on English pages, that native dialogs not
be wrapped, that the deploy default be resolved per call, and that tests and
docs cover these contracts and the template/script strings. Uses only the
existing [data-i18n-skip] marker; no new translation concepts.

Changes:

1. src/front/static/global/js/i18n.js
   Removed the alert / confirm / prompt wrappers (showNotification /
   showConfirmDialog output is already covered by the MutationObserver).
   Language cookie gets Secure on https. createTranslator exposed on
   OB_I18N_CORE for the DOM tests. Header comment documents data-i18n-skip.
2. src/front/fastapi/dependencies.py
   default_ui_lang() reads ONTOBRICKS_UI_LANG per call (was bound at import
   as DEFAULT_UI_LANG); resolve_ui_lang() falls back to it.
3. src/front/templates/base.html
   The i18n-<lang>.js dictionary is only emitted when the resolved language
   is not English.
4. src/front/templates/** (34 templates)
   data-i18n-skip on 53 user-content containers: ontology tree / lists / map,
   mapping lists and map, graph explorer panels, chat transcripts, result
   tables, registry lists, domain versions / discussions / documents /
   metadata / tasks, Neo4j connections, UC file lists, lock / table names.
   Static loading / empty-state text inside these containers is now left in
   English as well.
5. src/front/static/{ontology,mapping,query,domain}/js/*,
   global/js/comments-panel.js
   data-i18n-skip on script-rendered user names: entity / relationship panel
   titles (static titles like "Select Item" stay translatable), attribute
   names, bridge targets, graph switcher, comment author / body / tags. The
   manual-mapping title and table-details title get the marker from JS only
   while they show a name.
6. src/front/static/global/js/i18n-ko.js
   190 new entries for template and script strings found by the new coverage
   test (confirm dialogs, audit events, review workflow, analytics metrics,
   About / Help copy).
7. tests/units/front/test_i18n.py, tests/fixtures/i18n_mini_dom.js,
   tests/units/front/i18n_untranslated_baseline.json
   pytestmark unit; env-monkeypatched default-language tests; rendered-page
   tests that English pages omit i18n-ko.js and Korean pages load it; DOM
   tests on the real translator (mini DOM, no jsdom) proving a "Save" label
   and its title inside a skip region stay English, including nodes added
   later; contract that every listed user-content root carries
   data-i18n-skip; a coverage ratchet over template text / attributes and
   showNotification / showConfirmDialog / title / message / label literals
   against a committed baseline (product names, code tokens, fragments), with
   a stale-entry check.
8. docs/user-guide.md, docs/deployment.md, README.md
   Interface language section (navbar for every user, Settings card for
   admins, per-browser cookie, what is never translated); APP_UI_LANG ->
   ONTOBRICKS_UI_LANG row in the deploy config table; README note.

Modified files:
- src/front/static/global/js/i18n.js
